{"name":"Caput Mortuum","hex":"#592720","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caput mortuum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Worthless residue of sublimation or distillation.","Cardinal purple, a variety of haematite iron oxide pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caput_mortuum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caput mortuum","blocks":[{"text":"Caput mortuum is a Latin term used in alchemy to signify a useless substance left over from a chemical operation such as sublimation and the epitome of decline and decay. Alchemists represented this residue with a stylized human skull, a literal death's head."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caput_mortuum","wikidata":"Q421089"},{"title":"Caput mortuum (pigment)","blocks":[{"text":"Caput mortuum, also known as cardinal purple, is the name given to a purple variety of hematite iron oxide pigment, used in oil paints and paper dyes. Due to the cultural significance of its deep purple colour, it was popular for painting the robes of religious figures and important personages, with its popularity peaking in the 18th and 19th centuries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Ferric_oxide.jpg/330px-Ferric_oxide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caput_mortuum_(pigment)","wikidata":"Q96374414"},{"title":"Caput baroniae","blocks":[{"text":"In the customs and laws of the kingdom of England, the caput baroniae was the ancient, or chief, seat or castle of a nobleman — the primary place of his baronial court. The caput baroniae was not to be divided between multiple daughters ; instead, the whole of it was to descend entirely to the eldest daughter caeteris filiabus aliunde satisfactis, 'other daughters having been satisfied elsewhere'."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caput_baroniae","wikidata":"Q5037148"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShades_of_red.png"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Vase with lamps, Brown and beige textures, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/500px-Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg","ratio":1.5049019607843137,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vase_with_lamps,_Brown_and_beige_textures,_Rostov-on-Don,_Russia.jpg","share":0.09875},{"title":"Ford Madox Brown - The Last of England - Google Art Project","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","ratio":0.8934045986284792,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ford_Madox_Brown_-_The_Last_of_England_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","share":0.095},{"title":"Portrait of Francesco Maria de' Medici in armour","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Portrait_of_Francesco_Maria_de%27_Medici_in_armour.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Francesco_Maria_de%27_Medici_in_armour.jpg","ratio":0.7843137254901961,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Francesco_Maria_de%27_Medici_in_armour.jpg","share":0.089375},{"title":"Biblioteka z cyklu Mitologia czerwieni","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Biblioteka_z_cyklu_Mitologia_czerwieni.jpg/500px-Biblioteka_z_cyklu_Mitologia_czerwieni.jpg","ratio":0.34194068993342747,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biblioteka_z_cyklu_Mitologia_czerw